CORE
Test
--function Test.test2 --slice-formula --cp `../../../../scripts/format_classpath.sh . ../../../lib/java-models-library/target/core-models.jar ../../../lib/java-models-library/target/cprover-api.jar`
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
--
--slice-formula must not remove the assignment whose right-hand side is a
cprover_string_* function application: its constraints define the result
string's length and characters, which are passed as arguments, while the
assigned return code is never read. Before the fix, slicing dropped it and the
assertion failed spuriously.
